cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BN Lab in teaching material, a publication or a talk, please cite it as below."
title: "BN Lab: interactive physics and mathematics that actually compute"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free JavaScript library of interactive simulations for the web:
  forty experiments across chaos, waves, optics, quantum mechanics, relativity,
  statistical mechanics, automata and optimisation, plus a GPU Navier-Stokes
  fluid solver. Each experiment integrates its own equations in the browser, and
  a validation suite checks the on-screen numerical schemes against published
  and exact results.
